Troubleshooting steps :

A) Verify your Service
kubectl get svc

Node Port type and port number 

B) Check if pods are ready and not in CrashLoopBackOff, ImagePullBackOff, Pending
kubectl get nodes -o wide

C) Check the Endpoints
kubectl get endpoints or kubectl describe svc go-web-app-service

If you see Endpoints: <none>

then your Service selector does not match your Pod labels.

-> Check service selector 

kubectl describe svc go-web-app-service

-> Check POD label

kubectl get pods --show-labels

On checking my file, the POD selector did not match service label, edited both 

Issue : Security group issue

Resolution :
Added - port 31924 in the inbound of the ec2 instance (EKS nodes) SG where source is laptops public ip address obtained by browsing "whats my ip address" in browser

